    "body": "# Terrascope — AI Emissions Analyst\n\n## What It Is\n\nTerrascope is an **AI emissions analyst that calculates your greenhouse-gas footprint and files the regulatory report for you**. It walks you through what counts as Scope 1, 2, and 3 emissions for your business, gathers the right data, runs the math, and produces a report ready to file under the rules that apply to you.\n\nIt runs as a subscription. You don't have to learn the GHG Protocol, hire a sustainability consultant, or build a carbon-accounting spreadsheet — you answer the questions Terrascope asks, and it produces the deliverable.\n\n## Who It's For\n\nBusinesses that need to file a climate or emissions report under a regulation, but don't have a dedicated sustainability team. Today that primarily means:\n\n- **California.** Companies subject to **SB 253** (emissions disclosure for large in-state operators) or **SB 261** (climate-related financial-risk disclosure for mid-revenue companies). Also **CARB Mandatory Reporting** for facility-level filers.\n- **European Union.** Companies in scope of **CSRD / ESRS E1** climate reporting, or covered by the **EU ETS**.\n- **Voluntary disclosures.** Businesses preparing TCFD-style or investor-facing climate statements ahead of formal mandates.\n\nCoverage expands as more jurisdictions adopt mandatory disclosure rules.\n\n## How It Works\n\n1. You tell Terrascope what your business does, where it operates, and which rules you're filing under.\n2. Terrascope guides you through the data it needs — fuel use, electricity, refrigerants, business travel, supply-chain spend, and the other Scope 1/2/3 inputs that apply to your operations.\n3. It runs the calculations using the methodology required by your filing (GHG Protocol, IPCC factors, jurisdiction-specific overlays).\n4. It produces a filing-ready report and walks you through what to attach where.\n\n## Key Features\n\n- **Scope 1, 2, and 3 coverage.** Direct emissions, purchased energy, and the value-chain categories that apply to your business.\n- **Jurisdiction-aware.** Knows the differences between California (SB 253, SB 261, CARB MRR) and EU (CSRD, ESRS E1, EU ETS) reporting requirements; uses the right methodology for each.\n- **Conversational data collection.** Asks for data the way a human analyst would, not a 200-row spreadsheet.\n- **Filing-ready output.** Reports formatted to the structure each regulation expects.\n- **Numbers come from a calculator, not the AI.** Every emission figure Terrascope shows you originates from a deterministic calculation against published emission factors — not from a language model guessing.\n\n## Plans\n\nPlans are per-organization, per-year, sized to the complexity of the filing. See the plan pages for what's included at each tier.\n\n## Common Questions\n\n*FAQ pages link here as they're written.*\n\n## Related\n\n- [[products/frontdesk|FrontDesk]] — Neuvetra's other specialist (AI receptionist).\n- [[overview|Neuvetra overview]] — what Neuvetra is at the brand level."
